{"schemaName":"details","elementTitle":"More practice tips","fadeOverlay":false,"contentTitle":"About \"Open Math\"","link":"/page/faq/#-more-practice-advices","proseElement":{"__JSPROSE_element":true,"schemaName":"mix","children":[{"__JSPROSE_element":true,"schemaName":"list","data":{"type":"ul"},"children":[{"__JSPROSE_element":true,"schemaName":"listItem","children":[{"__JSPROSE_element":true,"schemaName":"paragraph","children":[{"__JSPROSE_element":true,"schemaName":"text","data":"So you (think you have) solved the problem. Follow the chain of buttons under the problem, from left to right: \"Check\" → \"Hint\" → \"Answer\" → \"Solution\". Do not rush to open, for example, \"Answer\" immediately. First, try to pass the \"Check\" a couple of times, use \"Hints\"!"}],"id":"paragraph-tJnB5Bez0CRf"}]},{"__JSPROSE_element":true,"schemaName":"listItem","children":[{"__JSPROSE_element":true,"schemaName":"paragraph","children":[{"__JSPROSE_element":true,"schemaName":"text","data":"Even if you solved the problem correctly yourself, study its \"Solution\" regardless. It is important not only to get the correct answer, but also to understand the "},{"__JSPROSE_element":true,"schemaName":"emphasis","data":{"type":"bold"},"children":[{"__JSPROSE_element":true,"schemaName":"text","data":"right train of thought"}],"id":"emphasis-vxCInMvBxUk2"},{"__JSPROSE_element":true,"schemaName":"text","data":" that leads to it!"}],"id":"paragraph-s2IP9c3rbMqy"}]},{"__JSPROSE_element":true,"schemaName":"listItem","children":[{"__JSPROSE_element":true,"schemaName":"paragraph","children":[{"__JSPROSE_element":true,"schemaName":"text","data":"Be sure to read \"Notes\" to problems! They contain important conclusions, generalizations, or interesting facts."}],"id":"paragraph-LStjCFTr93dL"}]},{"__JSPROSE_element":true,"schemaName":"listItem","children":[{"__JSPROSE_element":true,"schemaName":"paragraph","children":[{"__JSPROSE_element":true,"schemaName":"text","data":"If you cannot repeat the solu